<p>and common equivalent shares</p>
<p>   outstanding		   13,679  13,603   13,733   13,280</p>
<p>NOTE: The Company recognized a third quarter charge of $9.8 million to establish a reserve for certain Medicaid receivables due from the District of Columbia.</p>
<p>The Company incurred a net charge against earnings of $2.55 million to restructure certain business activities.</p>
<p>Additionally $0.75 million of the restructuring charge was for severance and termination costs associated with the discontinuation of the Company's facilities development and maintenance division, operated as Sterling Communities Corporation.</p>
<p>Additionally, operating income was adversely affected by additional costs of about $1.5 million associated with the completion of several government projects, moving costs associated with the Company's utilization management firm, including leasehold write-offs, and incremental costs associated with the New Jersey ISOC.</p>
